-- NOT a type error: this term is perfectly well typed at Nat, and it loops
-- forever.  MoreSTLC with fix is Turing complete, so a type checker cannot
-- rule this out -- type safety says a well typed term never gets STUCK, not
-- that it terminates.
--
-- Run it only if you want to watch your evaluator spin (Ctrl-C to stop).
-- It type checks instantly with:
--   morestlc --type-only examples/bad/diverges.mstlc
fix (\x:Nat, x)
